            02 · The journey
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">
            Student.
            <span class="text-white/30">Developer.</span>
            Creator.
            <span class="text-white/30">Founder.</span>
          </h2>

          <p class="mt-7 text-lg leading-8 text-white/50">
            My journey has never followed one straight line. Each stage taught
            me something that eventually became part of the way I build today.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-16 space-y-4">

          <article class="grid gap-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-[#080808] p-7 sm:p-9 lg:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white/40">
                01
              </p>

              <p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-white/25">
                Education
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
                From science to software
              </h3>

              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-8 text-white/45">
                My academic journey started with a B.Sc. in Mathematics,
                Physics and Chemistry. That background gave me a strong
                foundation in analytical thinking, problem solving and
                understanding systems.
              </p>

              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-8 text-white/45">
                I later pursued an MCA, moving deeper into computer science,
                software development and modern technology.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>


          <article class="grid gap-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-[#080808] p-7 sm:p-9 lg:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white/40">
                02
              </p>

              <p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-white/25">
                Development
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
                Learning by building
              </h3>

              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-8 text-white/45">
                Instead of limiting myself to tutorials, I started building
                projects — websites, JavaScript experiments, Python
                applications, database-driven systems, APIs and full-stack
                applications.
              </p>

              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-8 text-white/45">
                That approach became one of the most important parts of my
                development philosophy:
              </p>

              <p class="mt-4 font-medium text-white/75">
                Learn it. Build it. Break it. Fix it. Improve it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>


          <article class="grid gap-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-[#080808] p-7 sm:p-9 lg:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white/40">
                03
              </p>

              <p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-white/25">
                Full Stack
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
                From pages to complete systems
              </h3>

              <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-8 text-white/45">
                As my skills grew, I moved from individual pages to complete
                applications and started working across frontend, backend,
                databases, APIs and deployment.
              </p>

              <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                {[
                  "JavaScript",
                  "React",
                  "Next.js",
                  "Node.js",
                  "Express",
                  "MongoDB",
                  "MySQL",
                  "PostgreSQL",
                  "Python",
                  "Java",
                  "Spring Boot"
